# A twelfth Russian story: white nights
subtitle: "June in Petersburg: the sky stays light, the bridges over the Neva go up, and Masha and Tom are on the wrong side of the river. Eighteen lines to read and hear, then six questions by eye and by ear."
tags: ["russian","russian reading","russian story","white nights","petersburg"]
teaches: ["reading/reading-stories"]
thumb: "band \"A twelfth Russian story\" note \"white nights\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"A formal letter in Russian: уважаемый…","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/121-russian-formal-letter.cast"}

